{{- /*
Launcher for the `zellij terminal` desktop app (Zellij 0.46+), replacing the
one Zellij's own first-run setup writes. That setup copies whatever binary is
running to ~/.local/bin/zellij and points the launcher at the copy, which is
then frozen: `czup` upgrades the mise install but never the copy, so the
desktop app and the CLI drift onto different versions (and different
versions can't talk over the shared session socket dir), and the copy is an
unmanaged binary outside mise that the [user_tools] collision check flags.

Instead this points at mise's `latest` symlink, which `mise upgrade` moves,
so the desktop app always runs the same binary as the shell. The directory
name is mise's mangling of the [user_tools] key
"github:zellij-org/zellij" -- change both together.

No X-Zellij-Installed / X-Zellij-Fingerprint marker on purpose: Zellij only
auto-repairs or rewrites a launcher whose marker is intact, so without one it
treats this file as the user's and leaves it alone. Only deployed on profiles
with gui = true (see .chezmoiignore).
*/ -}}
{{- $zellij := joinPath .chezmoi.homeDir ".local/share/mise/installs/github-zellij-org-zellij/latest/zellij" -}}
[Desktop Entry]
Version=1.0
Type=Application
Name=Zellij
GenericName=Terminal Workspace
Comment=Manage Your Terminal Applications
Exec={{ $zellij }} terminal
TryExec={{ $zellij }}
Icon=dev.zellij.Zellij
Terminal=false
StartupNotify=true
StartupWMClass=dev.zellij.Zellij
Categories=System;TerminalEmulator;
Keywords=terminal;multiplexer;shell;workspace;
X-TerminalArgExec=-e
X-TerminalArgDir=--working-directory=
X-TerminalArgHold=--hold
X-ExecArg=-e
Actions=inbox;sessions;new-window;

[Desktop Action inbox]
Name=Show Inbox
Exec={{ $zellij }} terminal --inbox

[Desktop Action sessions]
Name=Show Sessions
Exec={{ $zellij }} terminal --sessions

[Desktop Action new-window]
Name=New Window
Exec={{ $zellij }} terminal
